# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Prettier already enforces endOfLine=lf on commit, but without this file Git
# for Windows' installer default (core.autocrlf=true) checks the tree out CRLF,
# and two things break: .husky/pre-commit runs `pnpm lint-staged\r` (sh keeps
# the carriage return as part of the word), and `pnpm schema:docs:check`
# compares prettier's LF output against a CRLF file and reports drift on every
# run. `eol=lf` applies regardless of the developer's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
